{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"ddead267b6c8fa96fe678d67a6f82cc42fbdc4bc1bc584c1a8a9a51e9169cd56","slug":"medium-mixtures","location":"/explanation/medium_mixtures.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Medium Mixtures","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/open223/docs.open223.info","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/open223/docs.open223.info/blob/main/explanation/medium_mixtures.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/open223/docs.open223.info/edit/main/explanation/medium_mixtures.md","thumbnail":"/build/mixed_medium-91a6c0dc9320c7e5aff24570c3dce1fb.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"medium_mixtures.md","url":"/build/medium_mixtures-571a95c65faf502fc1f3464580503ce5.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The 223 standard includes a large set of enumerations, defined as a hierarchy of subclasses under the class ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"z04SWobLba"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:EnumerationKind","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:EnumerationKind","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"izujURPMbV"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:EnumerationKind","key":"Jc35NgBqdm"},{"type":"text","value":".\nOne important piece of this hierarchy is the class ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"FOnGdn5BM1"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:EnumerationKind-Substance","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:EnumerationKind-Substance","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"xB72BCXmis"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:EnumerationKind-Substance","key":"OrJsXOFYG0"},{"type":"text","value":" and its direct subclass ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"Hzni3muQcU"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Substance-Medium","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Substance-Medium","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"UGwzSriKj2"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Substance-Medium","key":"xxbKvPdUfu"},{"type":"text","value":".\nIt is this branch of the hierarchy where you can find what you would expect to be flowing in a building, such as water, air and electricity. It is important to understand how a medium is modeled, especially when that medium is a mixture. The diagram below sketches the structure of the hierarchy. The names of the classes are abbreviated for clarity, so ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"gwMTjtknNR"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Substance-Medium","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Substance-Medium","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"pn1FKoTlQr"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Substance-Medium","key":"mRRBwT7ALW"},{"type":"text","value":" is shown as Medium for example. In the standard, each of the names follows the hyphenated naming convention of <parent class>-<local class>.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"DkFyI3bj4m"}],"key":"gvZGQBEXoS"},{"type":"image","url":"/build/mixed_medium-91a6c0dc9320c7e5aff24570c3dce1fb.png","alt":"MixedMedium","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"pe043mma8c","urlSource":"images/mixed_medium.png"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note in the figure that there is a division of the Medium class into Mix and Constituent. The Mix class is further divided into Fluid and Power&Signal. Fluid means what you might think - a liquid or gas that typically flows inside some sort of conduit like a duct or a pipe. You can find Water and Air here. To capture the description of what is in a mixture, the model contains the class Constituent and its subclasses. These subclasses are intended to identify the constituents of a mixture. So, for example, a water-glycol mixture would be defined as ","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"Xuv8KTskn0"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Water-GlycolSolution","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Water-GlycolSolution","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"nVmgA7kjQ8"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Water-GlycolSolution","key":"slDf7x7HYU"},{"type":"text","value":", with two Properties via the relation ","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"pe72Ez2HM5"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:composedOf","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:composedOf","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"iW7ISm2BHR"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:composedOf","key":"TcfkGHk1g8"},{"type":"text","value":". Each of these Properties has a relation ","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"rhfWKi33P8"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:ofConstituent","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:ofConstituent","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"MQOAISCznT"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:ofConstituent","key":"aKX53GCZQW"},{"type":"text","value":" that identifies one of the constituents from the Medium-Constituent hierarchy. Each Property also captures any other defining information. This is illustrated in the following figure for a 30%  Water-Glycol mixture.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"BdYvYreeFT"}],"key":"EPqqBC3iuS"},{"type":"image","url":"/build/glycol_example-4b732ddf682722ba4bd55505e76e5f5c.png","alt":"GlycolExample","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"BMpNvRrHzm","urlSource":"images/glycol_example.png"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mixtures (","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"ZhmPiIXCkL"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Medium-Mix","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Medium-Mix","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"tpEQVjhe8c"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Medium-Mix","key":"MDxLPSuMWq"},{"type":"text","value":") and constituents (","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"uzcxLjMBrK"},{"type":"link","url":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Medium-Constituent","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s223:Medium-Constituent","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"uAOESFSUZ6"}],"urlSource":"https://explore.open223.info/#s223:Medium-Constituent","key":"x2kOQkknza